# EBC APP — Project Structure

Full doc: `docs/engineering/standards/project-structure.md`

## Feature folder (required shape)

```
features/<feature-name>/
├── <FeatureName>.tsx
├── <feature-name>.types.ts
├── <feature-name>.constants.ts
├── <feature-name>.utils.ts        # if needed
├── use-<feature-name>.ts          # if needed
├── <FeatureName>.styles.ts        # or .module.css
├── components/<SubComponent>/     # sub-barrels for complex pieces
│   ├── <SubComponent>.tsx
│   ├── <SubComponent>.types.ts
│   └── index.ts
├── <FeatureName>.test.tsx
└── index.ts                       # feature barrel
```

## Barrel rules

```typescript
// ✅ import from module barrel
import { MemberDirectory } from '@/modules/members';

// ✅ import sibling subcomponent via its barrel
import { MemberRow } from './components/MemberRow';

// ❌ never cross modules via deep path
import { X } from '@/modules/members/features/member-directory/MemberDirectory';
```

- Each feature + shared UI folder has `index.ts` exporting **public API only**
- Do not export repositories from module barrels
- Prefer named exports; avoid `export *` except module root re-exports

## Routes stay thin

`src/app/**/page.tsx` only imports from feature/module barrels and passes params.
